---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';

const title = 'How to make a portfolio website';
const description = 'Make a portfolio website in seven steps: choose your work, write case studies, pick a template, add contact details and publish.';
const url = new URL('/guides/how-to-make-a-portfolio-website/', Astro.site).href;
---

<LegalPage accent="portfolio"
  kicker="Guide"
  title={title}
  seoTitle="How to make a portfolio website in 7 steps"
  description={description}
  updated="November 4, 2026"
  jsonLd={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: title,
    description,
    url,
    mainEntityOfPage: url,
    dateModified: '2026-11-04',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Vonex Design', url: new URL('/', Astro.site).href },
  }}
>
  <p>
    <strong>Short answer:</strong> pick your best three to six projects, write a short story for each, put them in a
    template and publish. Most of the work is choosing and writing, not design.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Decide who it is for</h2>
  <p>Write one sentence: what you do and who hires you. Use it as your headline. It also helps you decide which projects belong on the site.</p>

  <h2>2. Choose three to six projects</h2>
  <p>Pick the work you want more of. A short list of strong projects is easier to read than everything you have made. Check that you are allowed to show client work.</p>

  <h2>3. Write a short case study for each</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The client or goal, in one line.</li>
    <li>What you did, and what your role was.</li>
    <li>What changed after the work. Use a real result if you have one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Prepare your images</h2>
  <p>Collect images before you open an editor. Use one size and style for project covers, so the list looks consistent.</p>

  <h2>5. Pick a template</h2>
  <p>
    A template gives you the layout, responsive screens and project pages. Compare our
    <a href="/templates/category/portfolio/">portfolio website templates</a>. If you are not sure about the format, read
    <a href="/guides/framer-or-code/">Framer template or code</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Add an about section and contact details</h2>
  <p>Say what you offer, where you work and how to reach you. Keep one main contact option and show it on every page.</p>

  <h2>7. Check and publish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Open every page on a phone.</li>
    <li>Test the contact form and every link.</li>
    <li>Write a page title and description for search.</li>
    <li>Connect your domain and publish.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For a Framer walkthrough, see <a href="/guides/framer-portfolio-template/">how to build a portfolio with a Framer template</a>.</p>

  <div class="mt-xl flex flex-wrap gap-sm">
    <Button href="/templates/category/portfolio/" arrow>Portfolio templates</Button>
    <Button href="/guides/portfolio-website-examples/" variant="secondary" arrow>Portfolio examples</Button>
  </div>
</LegalPage>
